  "name": "Asian Pagoda",
  "category": "Traditional",
  "blurb": "Battered timber storeys under two stacked tiers of deep-eaved roof.",
  "teach": "Two Tiered Roof stages chained: the first is capped in height so it ends on a deck, and the second starts from that deck instead of replacing it. Chain a third and it keeps going. The tiers crown the building rather than covering every storey - a roof caps the whole massing, not each floor - so the lower eaves are a String course with its projection pushed out to half a metre, which is what reads as shelter at every level. The Mass carries a batter so each storey is smaller than the one below.",
